<title>LEBANON: Beirut bank mid-year profits up 72.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Beirut bank mid-year profits up 72.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Beirut net profits rose 72.53 percent to $4,096,200 in the first half of 1997, according to unaudited results issued by the bank on Thursday.</p>
<p>Net profits for the first half of 1996 were $2,374,000. They were $1,593,000 in the first quarter of 1997.  </p>
<p>BOB's share price has more than doubled since listing on the Beirut Stock Exchange on April 11 to $4.375 from $2.17.</p>
<p>The bank ranked 13th among Lebanon's 82 banks in terms of profits in 1996, according to Bank Data Financial Services.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 745307  745308  602057</p>
